\title{Equivalence class}
\date{2026-03-04T02:58:49Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{Let #{\sim} be an [equivalence relation](008Z) on #{A}, and let #{a \in A}. The \em{equivalence class} of #{a}, denoted #{[a]}, is the set of all elements of #{A} which are related to #{a}, that is, ##{[a] = \{ b \in A \mid a \sim b \}.}}


